# Apple Reminders

Use this skill for personal reminders that should live in Apple's Reminders app.
This is separate from Codex automations: use Codex automations when the user wants
this thread to wake up, monitor something, or run agent work later.

## Rules

- Use `osascript` against the macOS Reminders app.
- Treat dates as local machine time unless the user gives another timezone.
- For relative dates, resolve them to an exact calendar date before creating the reminder.
- Prefer a one-time Apple reminder for a one-time personal nudge when the user explicitly asks for Apple/iCloud.
- Do not create duplicate reminders. Search by exact title and reminder date first.
- After creating, updating, or deleting, read back the reminder state and report the exact title/date.
- If Reminders automation permission is blocked, tell {{USER_NAME}} the specific permission blocker and do not fall back to Codex automation unless he asks.

## Create A Reminder

Use this pattern. Construct the date by fields instead of a natural-language
`date "..."` string; it is less locale-sensitive.

```bash
osascript <<'APPLESCRIPT'
set reminderDate to current date
set day of reminderDate to 1
set year of reminderDate to 2026
set month of reminderDate to June
set day of reminderDate to 14
set time of reminderDate to 9 * hours

tell application "Reminders"
    set targetList to default list
    set existingMatches to reminders of targetList whose name is "Review upcoming deadline"
    repeat with r in existingMatches
        if remind me date of r is reminderDate then
            return "exists | " & (name of r as text) & " | " & (remind me date of r as text) & " | " & (id of r as text)
        end if
    end repeat

    set newReminder to make new reminder at end of reminders of targetList with properties {name:"Review upcoming deadline", body:"Reminder created by LifeOps after {{USER_NAME}} requested a native Apple reminder.", remind me date:reminderDate, due date:reminderDate}
    return "created | " & (name of newReminder as text) & " | " & (remind me date of newReminder as text) & " | " & (id of newReminder as text)
end tell
APPLESCRIPT
```

Notes:

- `time` is seconds after midnight. Use `9 * hours`, `13 * hours + 30 * minutes`, etc.
- Include `body` only when extra context will help {{USER_NAME}} act.
- Use `default list` unless the user names a specific Reminders list.

## Verify A Reminder

Read back by exact title, then check the date.

```bash
osascript <<'APPLESCRIPT'
tell application "Reminders"
    set matches to reminders whose name is "Review upcoming deadline"
    repeat with r in matches
        if remind me date of r is not missing value then
            return (name of r as text) & " | " & (remind me date of r as text) & " | " & (id of r as text)
        end if
    end repeat
    return "not found"
end tell
APPLESCRIPT
```

## Delete A Reminder

Be exact. Match title plus date or id when possible.

```bash
osascript <<'APPLESCRIPT'
tell application "Reminders"
    set targetId to "REMINDER_ID_HERE"
    set matches to reminders whose id is targetId
    if (count of matches) is 0 then return "not found"
    delete item 1 of matches
    return "deleted | " & targetId
end tell
APPLESCRIPT
```

## Output Contract

Report:

- whether the reminder was created, already existed, updated, deleted, or blocked
- exact reminder title
- exact local reminder date/time
- reminder id/link when available
